ent": "I even tried some new foods!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.<br/> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"italic\"> -ed</span> or <span class=\"italic\">-ied.</span> <br/> Irregular verbs change in different ways.<br/> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask \u2026 ?</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Did</span> is the past form of to do."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did you have a good time?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about current actions; things happening NOW."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I am having a great time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He is traveling in Cost Rica."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You form the Present Continuous tense by using the be-verb and by adding <span class=\"italic\">-ing </span>to the base form of the verb. <br/> I AM goING <br/> She/He IS travelING <br/> They ARE buyING"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "market"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place where products are bought and sold"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The markets are filled with food!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about places in the city."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "crowded"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "filled with many people and things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The markets in San Jose are crowded."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ill "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling sick or not well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My coworker got ill after he ate the street food."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "street food"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "food you buy and eat on the street"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The street food on Baker Street is delicious. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "active "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describing a volcano that is likely to erupt"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Tomorrow we are going to visit an active volcano."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to recognize"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to identify something or someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are foods I don't recognize."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le03ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a short e-mail to your friend describing a city you visited."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 6-8 sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Simple Past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your e-mail aloud."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write an e-mail to a friend about a city."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write complete statements on a place I visited."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I report about events in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read the e-mail aloud."}]}], "type": "sena"}